# Build context filter for the repository root.
#
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile-path>.dockerignore for the Dockerfiles in deploy/docker
# (Dockerfile.api.dockerignore / Dockerfile.worker.dockerignore). This root copy exists because the
# classic builder only looks here, and because a stray `docker build .` from the repository root
# must not ship secrets or runtime data to the daemon either.
#
# Everything below MUST stay out of the context: build output is rebuilt inside the image, runtime
# data holds the music library, and secrets must never be sent to the Docker daemon.

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vs
.vscode
.idea
.opencode
.agents
*.user

# Documentation, reports and test suites
docs
tests
e2e
README.md
SECURITY.md
LICENSE
AGENTS.md
opencode.jsonc

# Build output (rebuilt inside the image, or produced by the pipeline before the build)
**/bin
**/obj
**/out
**/dist
**/node_modules
**/TestResults
**/*.trx
**/*.tsbuildinfo
artifacts
publish
*.log

# Runtime data, local toolchains and secrets - never sent to the daemon
storage
tools
backups
.env
.env.*
*.env
dev.secrets.ps1
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
*.cer

# Client projects are not part of the server images
src/android
src/desktop
